@page "/components/alert"

<PageTitle>Alert — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Alert</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A message about the page, not about a control. <code>role="alert"</code> is deliberately
    absent: that announces immediately and interrupts, which is right for something that just
    happened and wrong for something that was already on the page when it loaded.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="AlertBasic.razor"><AlertBasic /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Destructive</h2>
<Example Source="AlertDestructive.razor"><AlertDestructive /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Action</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    A link or a form, never a click handler — so it works before any JavaScript, and a middle
    click opens it in a tab.
</p>
<Example Source="AlertAction.razor"><AlertAction /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Custom Colors</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Two variants ship; a third is a class rather than a new variant. Tint with theme tokens and
    the alert follows a theme change; tint with a literal colour and it does not.
</p>
<Example Source="AlertCustomColors.razor"><AlertCustomColors /></Example>

